==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_SuccessRequiresPermission  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_SuccessRequiresPermission.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets Alloy invent a successful Operation whose (callerRole, opKind) pair is NOT in the permission matrix — for example, a Member successfully invoking PatchAnyTask. LeastPrivilege explicitly requires (callerRole -> opKind) in PermMatrix.Allowed for every successful op, so it must surface the violation.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_009_NonOwnerMemberDenied
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_NonOwnerMemberDenied: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets Alloy create two distinct `Created` audit entries for the same task, which is exactly the situation AppendOnly (lone Created per task) is built to forbid.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipBasedAccess  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_OwnershipBasedAccess.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets Alloy invent a successful PatchOwnTask/DeleteOwnTask whose target is NOT owned by the caller, which is the bug OwnershipBasedAccess is supposed to catch.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_008_MemberEditsOwnTask
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_MemberEditsOwnTask: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CrossTeamIsolation  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_CrossTeamIsolation.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets Alloy invent a successful Operation whose target Task lives in a different team than the caller's contextTeam — the canonical multi-tenant leak NoInformationLeakage is built to forbid.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_011_AdminCannotCrossTeam, FR_014_CrossTeamByteEquivalent
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_AdminCannotCrossTeam: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_CrossTeamByteEquivalent: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditActorIsMemberWithRole  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuditActorIsMemberWithRole.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets Alloy create an AuditEntry whose recorded (actor, actorRole, inTeam) triple is NOT backed by any Membership row — i.e., misattribution. AttributionCorrectness requires a witnessing membership for every entry.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_015_AuditEntryShape
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditEntryShape: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnerIsTeamMember  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_OwnerIsTeamMember.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets Alloy invent a Task whose owner is NOT a member of the task's team, breaking the data-model.md guarantee that ownership is anchored in team_memberships.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipExclusivity, FR_006_TaskHasOneOwner
      - OwnershipExclusivity: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_TaskHasOneOwner: FAIL (expected)

